## Item 4: CHK-W2B3-26-003
Title: Verify Beacon Node Epoch Derivation from Current State
Severity: Critical | Bug Class: Input Validation | Mindset: Boundary Guard

### Primary Code (p2p/fork_watcher.go:forkWatcher lines 11-40):
```go
func (s *Service) forkWatcher() {
    if s.dv5Listener == nil {
        return
    }
    slotTicker := slots.NewSlotTicker(s.genesisTime, params.BeaconConfig().SecondsPerSlot)
    var scheduleEntry params.NetworkScheduleEntry
    for {
        select {
        case currSlot := <-slotTicker.C():
            currentEpoch := slots.ToEpoch(currSlot)
            newEntry := params.GetNetworkScheduleEntry(currentEpoch)
            if newEntry.ForkDigest != scheduleEntry.ForkDigest {
                nextEntry := params.NextNetworkScheduleEntry(currentEpoch)
                if err := updateENR(s.dv5Listener.LocalNode(), newEntry, nextEntry); err != nil {
                    log.WithFields(newEntry.LogFields()).WithError(err).Error("Could not add fork entry")
                    continue // don't replace scheduleEntry until this succeeds
                }
                scheduleEntry = newEntry
            }
        case <-s.ctx.Done():
            slotTicker.Done()
            return
        }
    }
}
```

### NetworkScheduleEntry / MaxBlobsPerBlock context:
- `forkWatcher` uses wall-clock slot ticks to derive current epoch
- `GetNetworkScheduleEntry(epoch)` returns the schedule entry with MaxBlobsPerBlock for that epoch
- ENR update includes the ForkDigest (which encodes BPOEpoch + MaxBlobsPerBlock for Fulu)
- The ForkDigest is XOR'd with hash(BPOEpoch || MaxBlobsPerBlock) for Fulu entries
- If ENR update fails, `continue` is executed (scheduleEntry NOT updated), so next slot tick re-tries
- The epoch derives from slot ticker (clock-based), NOT from chain state

